ion: Direction\n    amount: Amount\n\n    @property\n    def is_debit(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Indicates if this posting is a debit.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self.direction == Direction.INC\n\n    @property\n    def is_credit(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Indicates if this posting is a credit.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self.direction == Direction.DEC\n```\n\nAnd:\n\n```python\nclass Direction(Enum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides an enumeration of posting directions.\n    \"\"\"\n    INC = 1\n    DEC = 2\n```\n\nAnd JournalEntry.post:\n\n```python\n    def post(self, date: datetime.date, account: Account, quantity: Quantity) -> \"JournalEntry[_T]\":\n        \"\"\"\n        Adds a new posting to this journal entry.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.postings.append(Posting(self, date, account, Direction.INC if quantity >= ZERO else Direction.DEC, quantity))\n        return self\n```\n\nAnd ledger.py Ledger.add:\n\n```python\n    def add(self, posting: Posting[_T]) -> LedgerEntry[_T]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Adds a posting to this ledger.\n        \"\"\"\n        balance: Balance = Balance(posting.date, self._last_balance + posting.amount if posting.is_debit else self._last_balance - posting.amount)\n        entry: LedgerEntry[_T] = LedgerEntry(self, posting.journal, posting.date, posting.direction, posting.amount, balance)\n        self.entries.append(entry)\n        return entry\n```\n\nHmm, I'm not 100% sure whether it's `posting.amount` or `posting.quantity`. Since `Posting` has `amount: Amount`, it must be `posting.amount`.\n\nOK so to be safe with assertions, I'll assert:\n- `len(ledger.entries) == expected_count`\n- The final balance value: for a ledger with initial balance `b` and postings with positive quantities (INC direction), the last entry's balance should be `b + sum(quantities)`.\n\nActually, to be safest, I could avoid asserting exact balance arithmetic and instead assert structural things: entries count, entry dates, and